{{出典の明記|date=2015th year 8月}}
'''Shōgoi''' (正五位) is one of the Ranks in the [[:en:Japan|Japanese]] [[:en:Ritsuryō|Ritsuryō system]] and [[Shinkai (divine rank)|Shinkai (divine Ranks)]]. It is positioned below {{ill|Junior Fourth Rank|ja|従四位|1=Junior Fourth Rank|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fourth Rank|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fourth Rank|qq=}} and above {{ill|Junior Fifth Rank|ja|従五位|1=Junior Fifth Rank|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fifth Rank|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fifth Rank|qq=}}.<ref>https://www.wakapoetry.net/background/society/court-offices-titles-and-Ranks/court-Ranks/</ref> Posthumous Ranks for this level are referred to as ''Zōshōgoi''.

== Overview ==

Shōgoi, under the [[:en:Ritsuryō|Ritsuryō system]], was divided into upper and lower grades. In terms of {{ill|official Ranks|ja|官位|1=Kan'i system|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/official Ranks|13=User:Immanuelle/Kan'i system|qq=}}, it corresponded primarily to {{ill|Kyōkan|ja|京官|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kyōkan|qq=}} (capitals officers), especially positions such as {{ill|Benkan|ja|弁官|1=Benkan (administrator)|lt=Benkan|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Benkan|qq=}} ({{ill|Chūben|ja|左右中弁|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chūben|qq=}} or {{ill|Shōben|ja|少弁|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shōben|qq=}}) of the [[:en:Daijō-kan|Daijō-kan]], {{ill|Daibu|ja|大輔|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Daibu|qq=}} of the {{ill|Eight Ministries|ja|八省|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Eight Ministries|qq=}}, {{ill|Ōbanshi|ja|大判事|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōbanshi|qq=}}, {{ill|Ōzen-shoku|ja|大膳職|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōzen-shoku|qq=}} (Ōzen-daibu), [[:en:Major general|Shōshō]] of the {{ill|Konoe Guards|ja|近衛府|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Konoe Guards|qq=}}, and {{ill|Ōkan|ja|衛門府|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ōkan|qq=}}. These positions marked the middle-tier bureaucratic status.

In the {{ill|samurai|ja|武家|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/samurai|qq=}} class, the [[:en:Hōjō clan|Hōjō clan]] received this Rank during the [[:en:Kamakura period|Kamakura period]], while it was granted to [[:en:Daimyo|daimyō]] during the [[:en:Toyotomi clan|Toyotomi regime]]. However, during the [[:en:Edo period|Edo period]], appointments to Shōgoi decreased as focus shifted to {{ill|Jūshi'i|ja|従四位|1=Junior Fourth Rank|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jūshi'i|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fourth Rank|qq=}} and {{ill|Jūgoi|ja|従五位|1=Junior Fifth Rank|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jūgoi|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fifth Rank|qq=}}. In this era, the Rank was mainly awarded to {{ill|court officials|ja|宮廷|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/court officials|qq=}} like {{ill|Chikashōnin|ja|地下官人|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chikashōnin|qq=}} serving the [[:en:Royal court|Imperial court]], {{ill|Shinnōke|ja|親王家|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinnōke|qq=}}, {{ill|Gosekke|ja|五摂家|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gosekke|qq=}}, and {{ill|Seiga families|ja|清華家|1=Seiga families|2=ja|3=清華家|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Seiga families|qq=}}.

From the [[:en:Meiji era|Meiji era]], with the enactment of the {{ill|Rank Grant Ordinance|ja|叙位条例|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Rank Grant Ordinance|qq=}}, Ranks above {{ill|Jūshi'i|ja|従四位|1=Junior Fourth Rank|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Jūshi'i|13=User:Immanuelle/Junior Fourth Rank|qq=}} were granted by imperial decree, while Shōgoi and below were conferred by submission (奏授). This Rank often recognized mid-level samurai, [[:en:Military personnel|military officers]], and [[:en:Bureaucrat|bureaucrats]], especially those with notable contributions during the [[:en:Meiji Restoration|Meiji Restoration]]. Historical figures awarded the posthumous Shōgoi include [[:en:Mamiya Rinzō|Mamiya Rinzō]] (granted in [[:en:1904|1904]]) and [[:en:Kanezawa Sanetoki|Hōjō Sanetoki]] (granted in [[:en:1915|1915]]) for cultural accomplishments like founding the [[:en:Kanazawa Bunko|Kanazawa Library]].

Under the current system, Ranks are conferred posthumously as honors. Recipients often include distinguished [[:en:University|university]] and {{ill|college|ja|短期大学|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/college|qq=}} professors, [[:en:Business manager|business leaders]], {{ill|civil servants|ja|公務員|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/civil servants|qq=}}, and notable [[:en:Scholar|scholars]], {{ill|artists|ja|芸術家|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/artists|qq=}}, and {{ill|performers|ja|芸能人|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/performers|qq=}} who received awards like the {{ill|Order of the Rising Sun, Gold Rays with Neck Ribbon|ja|旭日中綬章|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Order of the Rising Sun, Gold Rays with Neck Ribbon|qq=}}.

